# ServiceNow identifier reporting

When working on ServiceNow scoped-app Git exports, **any time you create a new unique identifier**, tell the user:

1. **What the id is** — the exact value.
2. **Where it is** — file path and the field or element that holds it (e.g. row `sys_id`, filename, `targetId`, `definition.id`, `number`).

## Identifiers in scope

- Row **`sys_id`** (including when it drives the export filename `{table}_{sys_id}.xml`)
- **`number`** and other platform-generated unique fields on a record
- UX / macroponent ids — e.g. **`targetId`**, **`definition.id`**, **`definitionId`**, event or binding element ids when you assign new values

## When to report

- After creating or assigning a new id in code, XML, or JSON you edit
- After generating a new sys_id for a new record or artifact
- In your completion summary when the task introduced one or more new identifiers

Use a short, scannable list — one line per id — for example:

- `sys_id` `a1b2c3…` — `update/sys_script_include_a1b2c3….xml`, `<sys_script_include><sys_id>`
- `targetId` `d4e5f6…` — `update/sys_ux_macroponent_….xml`, event mapping `MACROPONENT_STATE_UPDATE_REQUESTED`

Do not skip this when ids are easy to miss (embedded JSON, multiple records in one file, or ids only in attributes).
